# An element's `$` field binds its dynamic (Type System ch. 4: a `$` field of an element
# binds a `$T`; neg live-field-bare): a pattern that would test the field's value,
# `$text=$"x"`, has no tick to test it in, since the element is live or a description, not
# a document's snapshot. prismc's back end refuses it today ("a pattern inside an
# element's `$` field"); the checker should. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering
# branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

IsX: fn Element Ui.* o -> Bool
fn IsX e = match e:
    Ui.Label($text=$"x"): True
    otherwise: False

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{IsX (Ui.Label($text=$"x"))}")
